# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere — in the repo AND in the working
# tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks files out as CRLF while
# storing LF. Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`, so `npm run format:check`
# reports dozens of files as unformatted locally while passing in CI (Ubuntu,
# LF). The committed content is identical either way, but a check that fails
# locally and passes remotely trains you to ignore it — which is exactly how a
# real formatting problem slips through.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.pdf           binary
